-- title:
--   A guard defect bounds target destruction together with same-row repairs
-- statement:
--   Suppose a zero-tolerance row accepts at t_j,g_j, both its targets are true at t_k, but it rejects at t_k,g_k. Let g_l≤g_k, and assume B(g_l,t_k)≤b_k, B(g_l,t_l)≤b_l and M(g_l,g_k,g_j)≤m. The union of its target-child downward flips at g_l and its repairs at target t_l, guard g_l, tolerance zero has size at most max(2b_k,2b_l+m).
